From 1524c99261ed163130671b07cec2b4fa9bdfe398 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 07:26:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Epic 7 Slice 7A.1: Configuration Registry (ADR-011)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Implements ADR-011: a thin, read-side registry that is the single source of
truth for Settings categories, removing the hardcoded category cards from the
Settings Home.

Layer 1 — static manifest (code, no persistence): one CONFIGURATION_MANIFEST
describing every category (key, type, title, description, group, order,
permission, owner, status, route, advisory dependencies/consumers), with
validateConfigurationManifest() enforcing unique keys/routes/order, valid
permissions and routes, and dependency hygiene — no graph traversal, cycle
detection, or dependency enforcement (advisory only).

Layer 2 — per-tenant read model + describe service:
describeConfigurationCategories(context, reader) joins the manifest to derived
tenant state, permission-filtered, tenant-scoped, in deterministic display
order, returning no configuration payloads. Status precedence:
coming_soon > available > configured/not_configured, with hasDraft and
hasScheduledChange as additive flags (never hiding the effective state).
"needs attention" is intentionally not emitted — no truthful read-side source.

Runtime state is read via one batched getConfigurationSummaries() (2 queries
regardless of category count; dates and booleans only), so Settings Home never
does per-category querying. No caching, no denormalized status, no new
persistence.

Settings Home and the card now render entirely from the registry; a pure
settings-navigation projection exposes the same list for any future sub-nav.
The global app navigation is intentionally left out of the registry.

Adds import-boundary fitness rules (registry must not import the write side;
manifest must not import persistence; clients must not import registry server
composition) with fixtures, plus a structural test that Settings Home has no
hardcoded category list. Adds ALL_PERMISSIONS/isPermission to context for
manifest validation.

Tests: +48 (manifest, service status/permission/tenant-isolation/ordering/no-
payload-leak, navigation projection, card presentation, Home structure).
Full suite 327 unit + 10 integration green; lint, typecheck, build, and
architecture-fitness pass; dev + production-mode browser flows verified.

